      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(dashboard): tunnel superseded Bay terminal cards to live retry",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Prioritize Bay terminal-buffer and recently-washed item keys in the bounded exact-review queue projection.\n- Let the existing Bay transition logic see a pending replacement review and suppress the superseded terminal failure/cancellation card.\n- Preserve the public 24-item sample bound and normal round-robin lane fill.\n\n## Problem\n\nExact-review workflow attempts that end in an expected held/superseded state can appear in Bay's terminal buffer while a newer durable-queue retry is pending. The public queue projection previously sampled independently, so it could omit that replacement item; Bay then had no active row to tunnel back into the earlier lane.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe status worker passes bounded, validated Bay item keys to the exact-review queue stats endpoint. The queue resolves those keys against live items before applying its public sample cap, then backfills the remaining slots round-robin. Stale terminal records cannot consume priority slots before a matching live retry is found.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm exec node --test test/dashboard-worker.test.ts` (144 passing)\n- `pnpm run build:dashboard`\n- `pnpm run lint:dashboard`\n- `pnpm run check:dashboard-queue-boundary`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check dashboard/exact-review-queue.ts dashboard/worker.ts test/dashboard-worker.test.ts`\n\nThe added regression coverage verifies a matching retry after stale Bay cards and confirms that priority rows still backfill to the 24-item public sample cap.\n\n## Review closeout\n\n- `codex review --uncommitted`: clean after addressing priority matching and sample-backfill findings.\n- `codex review --base origin/main`: clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n\n## Risks / rollout\n\nOnly the dashboard's bounded queue projection ordering changes; queue state, workflow dispatch, and publication behavior are untouched. Query keys are validated, deduplicated, and capped at 40 before reaching the durable object.\n",
